  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_481e470c08814d0caff41f52005bd52f",
      "statement": "Wire Center is the wire-transfer module of Crestline Business Online (CBO), CNB's commercial digital banking portal, providing domestic (Fedwire) and international (Swift) wire initiation, templates, dual approval, release with step-up authentication, an activity list, wire detail, CSV export, and confirmation PDF download.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L24-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6eb4e1fbf4a28ebb51b329886e3dba84d73bfd15ce56217f8416810cbee7689e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f059aa0922f047ef9dbe10009ee9d4ea",
      "statement": "Wire Center does not currently provide milestone tracking, Swift gpi international status, hold explanations, or client actions on held wires; gpi status is visible only to Payment Operations via the Investigations Workbench per spike CBO-4480.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L139-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01bb1daf51eabc17efc9fbb5ad3fbb7b5b526200953fcf793f69e265cb6cca30:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L24-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6eb4e1fbf4a28ebb51b329886e3dba84d73bfd15ce56217f8416810cbee7689e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8a3dbbc9dda438a9a335a578c3d415e",
      "statement": "Wire Center's logical architecture is a single React 18 / Aurora DS v4 MFE calling the cbo-wire-bff (Java 21 / Spring Boot 3 on OpenShift) over HTTPS with an OAuth2 session, with the BFF making synchronous REST calls to CES (entitlements), CBO Auth (step-up), PPH v1 (wire submission/list/status), and ENS (notifications).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L39-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ed39e07f6b48af7291442569c962064b7e091e9ce3598a928ff7ec23c00a01a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a1da38e0d8d14514896c9d633783c7b9",
      "statement": "Wire Center does not today use the CBO Status Projection Service (SPS, ACH only), the pay.wire.lifecycle.v2 event topic, PPH v2 APIs, gpi data, HMS APIs, or the TDIP Insights API.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L53-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6f08921b32fb9c914b873940a5da97b2ee3ce25808a7979c780e594492a3149:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e2ea2f09cc924dc880dca16b370bd4f5",
      "statement": "cbo-wire-bff's integration inventory comprises six calls: POST /pph/v1/wires (EP-PPH-03, submit, returns pphId stored with cboRef), GET /pph/v1/wires?clientId (EP-PPH-02, activity list, max 500 rows, client-side filtering per CBO-4302), GET /pph/v1/wires/{ref}/status (EP-PPH-01, wire detail status, cached 60s, throttled 1/60s per wire), GET /ces/v2/users/{id}/entitlements (EP-CES-01, authorization with account-level filtering), POST /cbo/auth/v2/step-up (EP-AUTH-01, step-up on release), and POST /ens/v3/notifications (EP-ENS-01, producing TRS.WIRE.* events).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L58-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:378b0397163114c7c5f188e3d53db7a7de7c61c602204ec2fb75cf64b4eac69e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L76-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:773e2ced1d440002e88c4ce074e8c912a7b351d5e5b4347be2f44af2f9893a2d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b892d87673c74568ad056a7f60ce31fd",
      "statement": "Wire Center derives its displayed client-facing status from the PPH v1 status field via a fixed mapping table (pre-submission CBO states Draft/Pending Approval/Approved; RECEIVED->Submitted; PENDING->In Process; HELD->Pending Review; PROCESSED->Completed; REJECTED->Rejected; CANCELLED->Cancelled; RETURNED->Returned), and the PROCESSED label was renamed from 'Processed' to 'Completed' in release R26.1 (CBO-4402) after client feedback that 'Processed' was unclear.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L80-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0404441262518543b59a77e054e8aefe0f39ba9f0898b26f9c760960aa1d64cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f498e832e9043baa1b3eb0869546ff3",
      "statement": "Held wires in Wire Center always display the generic label 'Pending Review' with fixed text 'This wire is being reviewed'; PPH v1 hold reasons (holdReasonDesc) are not shown to clients.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L95-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c9572b60da76a73ca7c96373d1e66f7c643333797a58bc5f4210425cf360d4e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17b911700c8249dbae900a1edd0a90c3",
      "statement": "Wire Center stores cboRef (its own primary key) and pphId (returned from the PPH v1 submission response) persistently, displays the Fedwire IMAD (from PPH v1 fedRef, per CBO-4355) without persisting it, and does not store or have access to OMAD or UETR because neither is available in PPH v1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L97-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6420fb0ce56b2ae672f80667d72792b80e17961d6afcc9ebca4b02f962358835:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_92cb4501ab8a4bd6ab817abfbfc9bb5f",
      "statement": "Wire Center produces three notification event types via ENS (EP-ENS-01): TRS.WIRE.APPROVAL_REQUIRED (template TPL-WIRE-APR-01; email/push/in-app) when a wire awaits approval, TRS.WIRE.RELEASED (template TPL-WIRE-REL-02; email/push/in-app/SMS opt-in) when PPH v1 status transitions to PROCESSED, and TRS.WIRE.REJECTED (template TPL-WIRE-REJ-01; email/push/in-app) on PPH v1 status REJECTED.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L107-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94cc22eab336aa0ae3d0741801269d37e1ff13ccd00cd112fc9aab6ee6139fdc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_669cfe3b8f864b14a787a2adb32d4d69",
      "statement": "Wire Center uses CES entitlement types WIRE_VIEW, WIRE_INITIATE, WIRE_APPROVE, WIRE_RELEASE, and WIRE_TEMPLATE_ADMIN; release requires step-up authentication (EP-AUTH-01) plus client-configured dual approval above client thresholds; external sharing of client transaction data is not supported without an InfoSec design review under SEC-STD-22 and a Privacy Impact Assessment; and search results are filtered to the user's entitled accounts inside the BFF.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L115-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9314e8a362dc5d298025d85bb0b858e81bff657b8e1c0af7aab9166ab91bca85:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b8804457e2f64575ac9c074202eeaae2",
      "statement": "Wire Center's five documented current-state constraints are: (1) no status polling permitted per ADR-PAY-019 following INC-2024-1182, only throttled user-initiated refresh (1/60s per wire), with new status capability required to be event-driven; (2) PPH v1 sunsets 2027-03-31 with migration tracked as CBO-4471 (34 points, unscheduled) depending on CBO-4473; (3) no international/gpi tracking, visible only to Payment Operations via Investigations Workbench; (4) the PPH v1 activity list caps at 500 rows with no cursor and no server-side beneficiary-name search; (5) the Status Projection Service (CBO-3815) is configured for ACH only, and wire support would require a new mapping module and a consumer ACL on pay.wire.lifecycle.v2.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L125-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc8e08d74cf1cc7957404831e55fd9e8e9f81c95d738a991d00e9409b8a28490:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4fef9f85be49418eb20c812a20717580",
      "statement": "Four reusable assets are identified as candidates for extending Wire Center rather than things it currently uses: the <cbo-journey-timeline> Aurora DS v4 component (origin CBO-3802, ACH Payment Tracker; rail-agnostic milestone timeline with terminal/error styling), the Status Projection Service (CBO-3815; Kafka consumer -> Postgres read model -> /cbo/sps/v1, extensible by config plus a mapping module), step-up authentication (CBO Auth v2, already used for wire release and reusable for other high-risk actions), and the ENS producer library (cbo-commons 3.x, templated sends with masking helpers).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L145-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6bae2df62938fe01d5a003589fb3d772a205add7087cc2989e126a3bf79d9156:"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
